   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Q1320** · question\n\nCan composite FMM formats (2a,3b,3c) with ZT > Q be upgraded to ZT={-1,0,1} strictly below live ZT via CLSS seam surgery or sub-block conjugation?",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "F1320_OBSTACLE",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**F1320_OBSTACLE** · fact\n\nDefault <4,3,3> row ordering (0,1,2,3) in 3x3x4_tensor.mpl has mixed inter-block overlap signs (up=5,um=4,wp=2,wm=5), creating +-2 seam entries on overlapping v-buds",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "L1320_SEAM56",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**L1320_SEAM56** · result\n\nLens 1 (seam-surgery-5to6): 5-to-6 ternary seam surgery + hybrid ZT bud selection gives verified ZT records 14x15x15<=1898 (vs 1905) and 10x15x15<=1392 (vs 1395)",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "L1320_CONJ",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**L1320_CONJ** · result\n\nLens 2 (subblock-conjugation-s3): Conjugating <4,3,3> by pi=(0,1,3,2) makes inter-block overlaps 100% sign-pure (up=0,um=11,wp=9,wm=0), yielding 4 verified ZT records: 9x12x14<=954, 10x15x15<=1389, 12x15x15<=1640, 14x15x15<=1894",
   "x": 840,
